 4736 L 1056 2765 L 1082 2765 Q 1203 3046 1424 3212 Q 1645 3379 2016 3379 Q 2528 3379 2825 3049 Q 3123 2720 3123 2118 L 3123 0 L 2611 0 L 2611 2029 Q 2611 2470 2422 2694 Q 2234 2918 1862 2918 Q 1658 2918 1472 2851 Q 1286 2784 1171 2643 Q 1056 2502 1056 2291 L 1056 0 L 544 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-31\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-b\" transform=\"translate(57.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-c\" transform=\"translate(114 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-16\" transform=\"translate(139 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e9\" transform=\"translate(187.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1c\" transform=\"translate(211.296875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-6\" transform=\"translate(260.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1\" transform=\"translate(315.609375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-15\" transform=\"translate(369.015625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p6402ac9b53\"><rect x=\"43.148281\" y=\"28\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"138.6\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Variable cost per m² ($)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Profit per m² fell from $2.90 to $2.40. Bridge:</p> <ul><li>Volume: +0.4M m² × $2.90 = <b>+$1.16M</b></li> <li>Variable cost: −$0.50 × 8.4M = <b>−$4.20M</b></li> <li>Fixed costs: <b>−$0.90M</b></li></ul> <p>Kiln energy is +$0.45 of the $0.50 rise per m², 90% of it, even though gas got cheaper.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> each m² now needs more energy. That points to how the kilns are used, not what energy costs.</p>","note":"Volume: 8.0M m² last year, 8.4M m² this year. Fixed costs: $18.0M last year, $18.9M this year."},{"q":"Every time a kiln line changes colour or size it burns about $1,800 of gas heating up and running off rejects. Otherwise energy costs $1.15 per m². What does that tell you about average run length?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Energy per m² = $1.15 + $1,800 ÷ run length.</p> <ul><li>Last year: $1.30 → $1,800 ÷ run = $0.15 → run ≈ <b>12,000 m²</b></li> <li>This year: $1.75 → $1,800 ÷ run = $0.60 → run ≈ <b>3,000 m²</b></li></ul> <p><b>So-what:</b> average runs are four times shorter. The custom orders fill the factory with changeovers: busy, but not productive.</p>"},{"q":"Selva could set a minimum run of 6,000 m² and batch custom orders weekly. What is that worth? How would you keep design customers?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>New energy per m² = $1.15 + $1,800 ÷ 6,000 = <b>$1.45</b>, saving $0.30 per m²: about <b>$2.52M a year</b>, before any lost orders. Profit would rise to about $3.8M.</p> <p>To keep designers:</p><ul><li><b>Small-run surcharge</b> priced at the changeover cost ($1,800 per run), so small orders pay their way</li> <li><b>Weekly custom slot</b>: collect orders and run them together</li><li><b>Stock a curated range</b> of popular \"custom\" colours</li></ul>","note":"Strong candidates price the surcharge from the changeover cost rather than inventing a number."}],"reco":"Profit fell from $5.2M to $1.26M because small custom orders cut average kiln runs from about 12,000 to 3,000 m², raising energy per m² by 35% even as gas got cheaper. I recommend a 6,000 m² minimum run with weekly batching of custom work, worth about $2.5M a year and lifting profit to about $3.8M, plus a small-run surcharge that covers the changeover cost and should close the rest of the gap to the $4M target. Risk: some designers go elsewhere, so offer a stocked custom range. Next step: re-plan two months of orders to confirm the run lengths are achievable.","great":["Finds that energy use, not energy price, is the issue","Back-solves run length from the cost formula","Prices the surcharge from the true changeover cost","Keeps the design customers rather than dropping them"],"id":24,"slug":"selva-ceramics"}